A final cluster of questions concerns foreign listings and Shanghai’s proposed international board. On the listing question Cha is unambiguous: $\text{List on NYSE or Nasdaq}
\Rightarrow
\text{subject to the full rules of that market}.$ A Chinese company can choose where to register and where to list. But once it lists in New York, it is subject to U.S. rules like any other listed foreign issuer. That is why Cha treats the place of listing, rather than the nationality of the underlying business, as the decisive regulatory fact.

